# The development box's own signing-key passphrase (config/dev-signing-passphrase.js).
# It is random per machine and it opens that machine's keys/private.pem, so it is a real
# secret even though it only ever exists on a dev box — committing it would publish the
# key material's password alongside the code that reads it.
.dev-signing-passphrase
# Cloud service-account private keys — NEVER commit. This platform integrates
# no Google identity or admin SDK (the Firebase Auth path was removed under the
# data-sovereignty requirement, e451fd04) and must never start; the patterns
# stay as defense-in-depth for the case where someone downloads a key file into
# the repo while investigating one. A key that reaches a commit is rotated, not
# deleted — see the project rules §8.
*serviceAccount*.json
*-adminsdk-*.json

