# STAGING-WALKTHROUGH capture kit — raw video/trace are large binaries and
# already ship via the CI artifact (14-day retention, staging-walkthrough.yml)
# or the operator's tar.gz pack (scripts/ops/run-walkthrough.sh). Screenshots
# + walkthrough-manifest.json stay tracked (evidence/<work-item>/ convention,
# the gacp-view-in-the-loop guideline) so they can go into the manual.
evidence/staging-walkthrough/test-output/

# FULL-GATE per-run logs — scripts/ci/full-gate.sh writes the ATTESTATION
# (evidence/gate/<sha>.json) and its per-check logs (evidence/gate/logs/<sha>/)
# into the repo. Only the attestation is an artifact anyone else needs: it is
# what scripts/probes/gate-attestation.sh and main-attestation-audit.sh read,
# so it stays TRACKED and the runbook commits it after every run.
#
# The logs are per-run diagnostics for whoever is standing at the machine.
# #845 made them survive cleanup() so they can actually be read there; that is
# the whole job, and it does not need git. Tracking them cost more than the
# bytes: the gate writes them DURING a run, so the next run's workspace-clean
# saw `?? evidence/gate/` and failed at check 1 — the gate dirtying the tree it
# checks, which cannot be escaped without committing megabytes of jest output
# between every run. Observed on VM-0-3-ubuntu 2026-08-08.
evidence/gate/logs/

# PROBE RUNNER per-run output — scripts/check-done.sh writes the result of the
# probes it just ran to evidence/probe-results.json. Same shape of problem as the
# gate logs above, and recorded once already at the change log: every run
# rewrites it, so the tree is dirty after every run and agents learn to
# `git checkout --` a guardrail's output by reflex.
#
# The 2026-08-07 fix made the PATHS inside it machine-independent, which was
# necessary but not sufficient: the CONTENT is a list of probe verdicts, and
# those legitimately differ per machine — no-secret is BLOCKED without gitleaks,
# suite-green needs a database. There is no version of this file that is correct
# everywhere, so a committed copy is a cached claim about probe outcomes that may
# not describe the commit someone is reading it next to. ci.yml:355 already
# records the session start script printing exactly such a cached copy instead of
# re-running.
#
# This does NOT stop it being evidence. the project rules §5 puts probe-results.json
# inside evidence/<work-item>/, where a pack keeps its own copy of the run it is
# attesting to — point PROBE_OUT_DIR at the pack. What is dropped here is only
# the floating copy at a fixed path that nothing reads across runs.
evidence/probe-results.json

# dependency-audit.sh per-run output (the raw `pnpm audit --json` it judged). Same
# reason as probe-results.json above: rewritten every run, differs per registry state.
# A pack that needs it points PROBE_OUT_DIR at itself.
evidence/dependency-audit.json
evidence/dependency-audit.json.err

